From bf62a16a54c63dd222fa205a01a9431683536693 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AuraLite <auralite@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:37:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] COMPAT G6: 4-vCPU BIOS SMP bring-up, MADT publication, and
 guest SMP tests

Tracing SeaBIOS 1.16.3-2's smp_setup() (0xf1538), smp_probe() (0xe8040),
handle_smp() (0xef526), and build_madt() (0xe9a3f) identified five
requirements beyond K6's --kernel SMP path for multi-AP BIOS bring-up:

1. Context capacity (src/machine.h, src/main.c): raise EM_MAX_VCPU from 2 to
   8, wire nv = min(cfg_smp, EM_MAX_VCPU) contexts with l.id = i << 24, and
   count remaining VCPU_RUN slots when an AP parks in VCPU_OFF.
2. CMOS 0x5F (src/rtc.c, src/main.c): set CMOS[0x5F] = nv - 1 when nv > 1
   (0 in UP) so SeaBIOS smp_probe() sets MaxCountCPUs = nv.
3. Broadcast INIT and SIPI (src/lapic.c): handle ICR destination shorthands
   2 (all incl. self) and 3 (all excl. self) on the dm == 5 (INIT) and
   dm == 6 (SIPI) path used by SeaBIOS smp_setup() (0x000C4500 / 0x000C4610).
4. Initial APIC ID in CPUID(1).EBX[31:24] (src/cpu.c): report
   m->lapic.id & 0xFF000000u in EBX[31:24] (0 on BSP/UP, i << 24 on vcpu_i)
   so SeaBIOS smp_write_msr() sets bit (1 << apic_id) in FoundAPICIDs and
   build_madt() marks all 4 Processor Local APIC entries enabled (flags=1).
5. Counter preservation across second-stage INIT (src/lapic.c): preserve
   executed_steps, instr_count, idle_quantum, and last_vtime across
   cpu_reset(&s->c) in vcpu_take_init() so the kernel's second-stage targeted
   INIT does not wipe an AP's SeaBIOS POST work counters.

Measured on --lpc=ich9 --smp=4 (docs/evidence/compat-g6/):
- Diagnostic SeaBIOS POST prints handle_smp: apic_id=0x1..0x3 and
  'Found 4 cpu(s) max supported 4 cpu(s)'.
- Full BIOS boot with stock Debian SeaBIOS 1.16.3-2 + the accepted ISO
  publishes a 134-byte MADT (cpus=4 ioapics=1 isos=4) and boot_info_t with
  cpu_count=4, wakes all 3 APs ('[smp] AP #0..#2 online', '[smp] 4 CPU(s)
  online (3 AP(s) woken)'), logs '[sched] R5 receipt: user thread pid=6 on
  AP cpu=3', reaches '[kernel] shell active; kmain idling.', and passes typed
  /tests/irqapwake ('RES-16 receipt', 'IRQAPWAKE PASS') and /tests/smpstress
  ('O_APPEND 6 x 200 x 32 B intact', '100 fork/wait cycles precise',
  '8 x 10 signal deliveries counted', 'SMPSTRESS PASS') with fault=0 on all
  4 vCPUs and exact work-counter identities (executed=1187467939,
  idle_quantum=180026141696, vtime=181213609635).
- Historical lanes (p5_history.sh 9/9 plus 40M --kernel UP and --cpus=2
  --smp=2) are byte-identical against the G5 binary.

Tests: test_cmos_smp_extra_cpus in tests/test_rtc.c,
test_smp_broadcast_init_sipi_and_counter_preservation in tests/test_lapic.c,
make test-g6 (73 bundle checks, in make test), make test-g6-nc (five tampered
bundles), and make test-g6-live (tests/integration/g6_smp_nc.sh).
